  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nFutures are bleeding red ahead of NFP, with NASDAQ leading the carnage down 2.92% as tech gets hammered. VIX spiking 5% to 24.68 signals real fear, while geopolitical tensions in the Gulf add fuel to the fire. Classic risk-off setup with money rotating into defensive sectors.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Non Farm Payrolls (8:30 ET)</strong> - The big kahuna today. Market's pricing in volatility with VIX elevated</li>\n<li><strong>Iran-US Naval Tensions</strong> - Iran fired warning shots at US warships in Gulf of Oman. Oil and defense plays on watch</li>\n<li><strong>Tech Sector Meltdown</strong> - XLK down 4.59% pre-market. Major support levels being tested across mega-caps</li>\n<li><strong>ABM Earnings (BMO)</strong> - EPS est 0.883, one of the few notable reports in a light earnings day</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClassic flight to safety underway with defensive sectors leading. Consumer Staples (+1.84%) and Healthcare (+1.68%) catching bids while Tech gets annihilated. Energy surprisingly weak despite Middle East tensions, down 1.38% as growth fears trump geopolitical risk premiums.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Tech breakdown accelerates if NFP comes in hot, forcing Fed to stay hawkish longer. Geopolitical escalation could trigger broader risk-off spiral into the weekend.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Jobs data at 8:30 ET will set the tone. Strong number = more Fed hawkishness = tech pain continues. Weak number = recession fears = different kind of selling.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 745</strong> - Currently testing this level pre-market. Break below targets 740 support</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ 715</strong> - Key technical level. Failure here opens door to 700 round number</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 25</strong> - Just shy of this psychological resistance. Break above signals real panic</li>\n<li><strong>XLK 180</strong> - Major support for tech sector ETF. Watch for volume on any bounce attempt</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
